    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1005">

                <pb facs="1143" n="1063" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg1063"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr.
                            Bowen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-04-22"><hi rendition="#italic">April 22,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr Hill states that it is represented that the Venezuelan consul at Port of
                    Spain, who refuses to clear the New York and Bermudez Company’s vessel for Caño
                    Colorado with food supplies for employees, declares that if the vessel proceeds
                    with papers signed by the United States consul he will send a gunboat to seize
                    her as a pirate.</p>
                <p>Mr. Bowen is directed to ascertain and report to the Department whether the
                    Venezuelan Government authorized its consul to make such a statement.)</p>
            </div>
